    "updated_at": "2023-11-22T10:29:35Z",
    "body": "We are releasing a hotfix removing `openqaoa-pyquil` from the global package temporarily and will work to resolve the issue.\r\nIn the meantime, this bug can be ignored by:\r\n- Installing plugins separately through PyPI: `pip install openqaoa-XXX`, where `XXX` can be replaced by `core`, `qiskit`, `braket`, `azure` but NOT `pyquil`.\r\n- Installing the package locally one plugin at a time: clone the repo, `cd openqaoa`, `pip install ./src/openqaoa-XXX`\r\n\r\nNote that `openqaoa-pyquil` can still be installed as a \"standalone\" package (still requires core).",
